%U A399409 105,104,95,83,63,40,14,77,100,116,125,128,124,112,94,72,44,18,89,115,135,146,155,153,145,130,108,82,52,19
%N A399409 Order array, U, of the array W given by w(n, k) = k*(n + sqrt(5)), for n >= 1, k >= 1, a rectangular array, read by descending antidiagonals; see Comments.
%C A399409 Suppose that (w(n, k)), for n >= 1 and k >= 1 is an array of distinct real numbers. Replace each w(n, k) by its position when all the numbers w(n, k) are ordered by < . The resulting array, U = (u(n, k)), is the order array of (w(n, k)). Every positive integer occurs exactly once, so that as a sequence this is a permutation of the positive integers. Successive row terms, and column terms, have limiting ratio 1. See A399406 for a guide to related arrays.
%H A399409 <a href="/index/Per#IntegerPermutation">Index entries for sequences that are permutations of the natural numbers</a>
%F A399409 u(n,k) = Sum_{h = 1..floor(k*(n+x)/(1+x))} floor(k*(n+x)/h - x), where x = sqrt(5).
%F A399409 u(n,k) = Sum_{m = 1..floor(k*(n+x) -x )} floor(k*(n+x)/(m+x)), where x = sqrt(5).
%e A399409 Corner:
%e A399409    1    5   10   17   23   32   41   49
